clustine-features

Parts of this crate are adapted from SteelMC
(https://github.com/Steel-Foundation/SteelMC), branch `26.3` at commit
`885c4b3e60ed79862c37311780774f76806cb714`. Steel: A high-performance Minecraft
server implementation written in Rust. Copyright (C) 2026 Alve Jeansson and
contributors. Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or
(at your option) any later version; see `LICENSE` at the root of this
repository. The files that were adapted say so at their head.

The placers of structures' pieces are adapted from SteelMC's
steel-core/src/worldgen/structure/piece_placer/, with what the pinned 26.3 jar's
classes do otherwise put right, each file saying which: src/structures/jigsaw.rs
(pool_element.rs); src/structures/template_piece.rs, src/structures/shipwreck.rs,
src/structures/igloo.rs and src/structures/ocean_ruin.rs (template_piece.rs and
template_processors.rs); src/structures/ruined_portal.rs (ruined_portal.rs and
template_processors.rs); src/structures/buried_treasure.rs (buried_treasure.rs).

The data the crate computes with is Mojang's, from `clustine-worldgen-data`; see
NOTICE.md at the root of the repository. No block of a structure template is in
this repository (ADR-0019).
